.TH SYSTEMD-MANAGER-TUI 1 "October 2026" "systemd-manager-tui 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
systemd-manager-tui \- terminal user interface for managing systemd services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-manager-tui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-manager-tui
manages system and user units through D-Bus from an interactive terminal.
It can control services, inspect properties, display journal logs, edit unit
files and create instances of template services.
System operations require the permissions enforced by systemd and D-Bus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filter " " \fITEXT\fR
Apply a filter on startup.
.TP
.B \-\-operation-timeout-secs \fISECONDS\fR
Maximum time to wait for a service operation to settle.
Must be at least 1; defaults to 10 seconds.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no-notifications
Disable notifications for failed system and user units.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the version.
.SH KEYBOARD
In the service list, use the up and down arrow keys or j and k to navigate.
Use the left and right arrow keys to switch between system and user units.
.PP
Press s to start, x to stop, r to restart, e to enable, d to disable,
and m to mask or unmask the selected service.
Press a to filter, f to toggle listing all units, and u to refresh.
Press v to view logs, c to view the unit file, and ? for help.
Press Ctrl+C to quit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
systemd-manager-tui \-f ssh
systemd-manager-tui \-n
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd (1)
